# Line endings.
#
# This repo mirrors a Linux server, so the bytes in the blob must equal the bytes
# deployed - tools/verify-deploy.sh compares them by md5. That was previously
# achieved with "* -text", which tells git to do NO conversion at all.
#
# The problem with "* -text" is that it also means git never NORMALISES anything.
# A file's line endings stay whatever they were when first committed, and an edit
# made on Windows commits CRLF silently. On 2026-08-01 that turned a 20-line
# change into a 195-line diff, and twice made a stale deployment look like it had
# drifted when the only difference was carriage returns.
#
# "text=auto eol=lf" is strictly better here: the blob is LF, and a checkout on
# Linux writes LF - so deployed bytes still equal blob bytes and the md5 check
# still holds - while anything edited on Windows is normalised on commit instead
# of poisoning every future diff of that file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never convert these. text=auto guesses from content and is usually right, but a
# wrong guess corrupts a binary silently, so the common types are declared.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svgz  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.mp4   binary
*.swf   binary
*.z     binary
*.dat   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.phar  binary
